      {
        "thread_id": "TH3",
        "thread_goal": "Align on the activity plan and how to support children emotionally during the new routine.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M37",
            "speaker_id": 508714,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi all, as per T4, I've drafted the Child Wellbeing Activity Plan (A4). It includes a mix of activities like sensory play, story time, and simple crafts. The goal is to provide predictability and emotional support. Please let me know if these are suitable for the different ages and conditions we see.",
            "mentions": [
              3328,
              47149,
              47214,
              427358
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T4",
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "art",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M38",
            "speaker_id": 3328,
            "reply_to": "M37",
            "text": "Thanks @508714, this looks great. I've cross-referenced it with our new routine in A3, and the timings for the 'structured activity' blocks fit perfectly. How do you suggest we adapt these for children who might be in isolation or have very low energy?",
            "mentions": [
              508714
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M39",
            "speaker_id": 508714,
            "reply_to": "M38",
            "text": "Good question. For each activity, I've included a 'quiet alternative'. For example, during craft time, a child with low energy could simply watch or choose colours, while a child in isolation could be given a self-contained kit. The focus is on inclusion without pressure.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bulb",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M40",
            "speaker_id": 47214,
            "reply_to": "M37",
            "text": "I like the ideas in A4. They seem easy to set up. Do we have all the supplies for these?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M41",
            "speaker_id": 508714,
            "reply_to": "M40",
            "text": "I've checked the inventory, and we have everything needed for the pilot week. I tried to use common, multi-purpose supplies.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M42",
            "speaker_id": 47149,
            "reply_to": "M37",
            "text": "The kids will like drawing.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M43",
            "speaker_id": 427358,
            "reply_to": "M37",
            "text": "This plan is really thoughtful. It also gives us something positive to talk about with the families. We can mention it during our checks.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M44",
            "speaker_id": 3328,
            "reply_to": "M39",
            "text": "The 'quiet alternative' is a brilliant solution. It ensures no child is left out. To make the pilot manageable, we should probably decide which activities are core to the routine and which are flexible. This will help staff who are new to the routine.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M45",
            "speaker_id": 508714,
            "reply_to": "M44",
            "text": "I agree. I propose that the 'Morning Circle/Greeting' and the 'End-of-Day Story Time' are mandatory. They bookend the day with a stable routine. The mid-morning and afternoon creative activities could be optional, depending on the children's mood and energy levels. How does that sound?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D5"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M46",
            "speaker_id": 3328,
            "reply_to": "M45",
            "text": "That makes perfect sense. It provides structure without being rigid. Let's lock that in. Decision D5: Morning Circle and End-of-Day Story Time are mandatory; other activities are optional during the pilot.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D5"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "white_check_mark",
                "count": 3
